# Observability

## Approved dependency

The app has **one** third-party SDK: **Sentry** (Cocoa, via SPM only). No Crashlytics, Firebase, Amplitude, or other analytics/crash SDKs.

Product analytics go to TelemetryDeck through first-party `URLSession` code (`AnalyticsClient`, `TelemetryDeckClient`), not its SDK. Events are bare counts from `AnalyticsEvent`. Payloads carry only app, OS, and device context (model identifier, orientation, screen size) and retention counts, under TelemetryDeck's SDK keys: never user content. Analytics failures log at `.debug`, not `.error`, so a TelemetryDeck outage does not flood Sentry. See [`OBSERVABILITY.md`](OBSERVABILITY.md#product-analytics).

- Add or upgrade Sentry only through the Xcode project’s package reference (`sentry-cocoa`). Do not add CocoaPods or Carthage.
- [`scripts/validate-rules.py`](scripts/validate-rules.py) fails if `project.pbxproj` references any other remote Swift package.
- The beforeShellExecution hook still blocks CocoaPods, Carthage, and ad-hoc `Package.swift` / `Podfile` manifests.

## What we capture

- Crashes, hangs, and release health (crash-free sessions) for TestFlight and App Store builds.
- Selective non-fatal technical events that already go through `AppLogging` at `.error` — category and a developer-authored message only.
- Release name must match shipping identity: `MARKETING_VERSION` + `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` from Info.plist (same numbers as `testflight/<marketing>+<build>`).

## What we never capture

Same bar as [`errors-logging.mdc`](.cursor/rules/errors-logging.mdc) and [`secrets.mdc`](.cursor/rules/secrets.mdc):

- No user content (search queries, list titles, favorites, notes, PII).
- No API keys, tokens, Authorization headers, or full request URLs (query strings can hold credentials).
- No Session Replay, screenshots, or view hierarchy dumps unless product explicitly opts in later.
- Do not set a Sentry user id to email, name, or any account identifier this app does not have.

## Secrets and init

- DSN lives in gitignored `Secrets.xcconfig` as `SENTRY_DSN`, surfaced through Info.plist. Template: [`Secrets.example.xcconfig`](Secrets.example.xcconfig).
- xcconfig treats `//` as a comment — write `SENTRY_DSN = https:/$()/…@….ingest…/…` (see the example file). `SentryBootstrap` also strips a leftover `$()` if it reaches Info.plist.
- Missing or empty DSN: do **not** start Sentry (local Debug without a project stays quiet). Release/TestFlight CI must supply the DSN.
- Start Sentry as early as practical in `AppDelegate` via `SentryBootstrap`, before other app work. No smoke-test `capture` / `flush` / DSN `print`s in committed app code.

## CI and symbols

- Upload dSYMs for every TestFlight archive (release workflow or `release.py`), or stack traces stay useless.
- Tie Sentry releases to the same marketing+build the archive verified.
